The domain is $-3\leq x\leq1$.
$\begin{aligned}\frac{dy}{dx}&=-\frac{\frac{x+1}{2}}{\sqrt{1-\frac{(x+1)^{4}}{16}}}\\\frac{dy}{dx}&=-\frac{2(x+1)}{\sqrt{16-(x+1)^{4}}}\end{aligned}$
At $x=-1$, $\dfrac{dy}{dx}=0$. The denominator is positive for $-3<x<1$.
For $-3<x<-1$, the gradient is positive. For $-1<x<1$, the gradient is negative.
The gradient changes from positive to negative, so $\left(-1,\dfrac{\pi}{2}\right)$ is a maximum turning point.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=1cm,y=1.4cm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\definecolor{mathblue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\draw[->,black] (-3.6,0)--(1.6,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->,black] (0,-0.2)--(0,2) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[mathblue,thick,domain=0:180,samples=101,variable=\t] plot ({-1-2*cos(\t)},{acos((cos(\t))*(cos(\t)))*pi/180});
\fill[black] (-3,0) circle (1.3pt);
\fill[black] (1,0) circle (1.3pt);
\fill[black] (-1,1.5708) circle (1.3pt);
\path (-3,0) node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$-3$};
\path (1,0) node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$1$};
\path (-1,1.5708) node[above left] {$(-1,\frac{\pi}{2})$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

examples.question_text:
A plane flies directly away from an observer at a constant altitude of $4$ km and a speed of $540$ km/h. Its horizontal distance from the observer is $x$ km and its angle of elevation is $\theta$. Find, in radians per second, the rate at which $\theta$ is decreasing when $x=4$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw[black] (0,0)--(0,2.4)--(3.6,2.4)--cycle;
\draw[black] (0,2.1)--(0.3,2.1)--(0.3,2.4);
\draw[black,dashed] (0,0)--(1.3,0);
\draw[black] (0.8,0) arc[start angle=0,end angle=33.69,radius=0.8];
\draw[black,->] (3.6,2.4)--(4.5,2.4);
\path (0,0) node[below left] {$O$};
\path (0,2.4) node[above left] {$A$};
\path (3.6,2.4) node[above] {$P$};
\path (0,1.2) node[left] {$4\text{ km}$};
\path (1.8,2.4) node[above] {$x\text{ km}$};
\path (4.1,2.4) node[below] {$540\text{ km/h}$};
\path (1.05,0.3) node {$\theta$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A picture $BT$ is $2$ metres tall. Its lower edge $B$ is $2$ metres above a viewer's eye $E$. The viewer stands $x$ metres from the wall, and the picture subtends angle $\theta$ at $E$.
a. Express $\theta$ in terms of $x$.
b. Find the distance from the wall that maximises $\theta$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw[black] (0,0)--(3.4,0)--(3.4,4);
\draw[black,very thick] (3.4,2)--(3.4,4);
\draw[black] (0,0)--(3.4,2);
\draw[black] (0,0)--(3.4,4);
\draw[black] (3.1,0)--(3.1,0.3)--(3.4,0.3);
\draw[black] ({1.1*cos(30.47)},{1.1*sin(30.47)}) arc[start angle=30.47,end angle=49.64,radius=1.1];
\path (0,0) node[below left] {$E$};
\path (3.4,0) node[below right] {$P$};
\path (3.4,2) node[left] {$B$};
\path (3.4,4) node[above] {$T$};
\path (1.7,0) node[below] {$x\text{ m}$};
\path (3.4,1) node[right] {$2\text{ m}$};
\path (3.4,3) node[right] {$2\text{ m}$};
\path (1.15,1) node {$\theta$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
